instruction:
Design a PLC program using structured text (ST code) that includes a function block named `F_CollectInput` and a main program named `MAIN`.

The main program begins by invoking the `CollectInput` function block to gather input signals (`IN1`, `IN2`, `IN3`, `IN4`, and `IN5`) into a Boolean array called `Data`. Once data collection is complete, indicated by the `Finished` flag from the function block, the program sets a `Ready` flag to signal readiness for further processing.

Upon readiness, the program calculates an output signal `Out` based on complex logical conditions:
NOT (A1 OR A2 OR A3 OR ... OR A15)  , where the A1 to A15 satisfy:

```plain
A1 = NOT (Data[7]) AND NOT (Data[3]) AND NOT (Data[2]) AND NOT (Data[1]) OR Data[5];
A2 = Data[7] AND NOT (Data[3]) AND NOT (Data[2]) AND NOT (Data[1]) OR Data[6];
A3 = NOT (Data[7]) AND Data[3] AND NOT (Data[2]) AND NOT (Data[1]) OR Data[12];
A4 = Data[7] AND Data[3] AND NOT (Data[2]) AND NOT (Data[1]) OR Data[8];
A5 = NOT (Data[7]) AND NOT (Data[3]) AND Data[2] AND NOT (Data[1]) OR Data[4];
A6 = Data[7] AND NOT (Data[3]) AND Data[2] AND NOT (Data[1]) OR Data[9];
A7 = NOT (Data[7]) AND Data[3] AND Data[2] AND NOT (Data[1]) OR Data[10];
A8 = Data[7] AND Data[3] AND Data[2] AND NOT (Data[1]) OR Data[16];
A9 = NOT (Data[7]) AND NOT (Data[3]) AND NOT (Data[2]) AND Data[1] OR Data[11];
A10 = Data[7] AND NOT (Data[3]) AND NOT (Data[2]) AND Data[1] OR Data[14];
A11 = NOT (Data[7]) AND Data[3] AND NOT (Data[2]) AND Data[1] OR Data[17];
A12 = Data[7] AND Data[3] AND NOT (Data[2]) AND Data[1] OR Data[18];
A13 = NOT (Data[7]) AND NOT (Data[3]) AND Data[2] AND Data[1] OR Data[13];
A14 = Data[7] AND NOT (Data[3]) AND Data[2] AND Data[1] OR Data[20];
A15 = NOT (Data[7]) AND Data[3] AND Data[2] AND Data[1] OR Data[15];
```

System evaluate the values stored in the `Data` array.
Then the output readiness flag `OutReady` is set to true, indicating that the system is prepared to produce the final output.

Finally, after the output is calculated, the program resets the `CollectInput` function block to prepare for the next
round of data collection by setting the `RESET` flag to true.

The program includes a function block named `F_CollectInput`,
which collects multiple input signals (`IN1`, `IN2`, `IN3`, `IN4`, and `IN5`)
into a Boolean array called `Data` during each cycle when triggered by a clock signal `TICK`.
The data collection occurs only when the `RESET` signal is not activated,
ensuring that the system captures inputs correctly.

When the system captures data, it stores the input values in `Data`,
updates the index for future data collection,
and sets the `Finished` output flag to indicate when the data array is fully populated (after 20 inputs).
If a reset is initiated, the index is reset, and the previous data collection is cleared,
readying the system for a new set of inputs.


FUNCTION_BLOCK F_CollectInput
VAR_IN_OUT
Data : ARRAY[1 .. 20] OF BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR_INPUT
TICK  : BOOL := 0;
IN1   : BOOL := 0;
IN2   : BOOL := 0;
IN3   : BOOL := 0;
IN4   : BOOL := 0;
IN5   : BOOL := 0;
RESET : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
Finished : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR
j    : USINT := 1;
tock : BOOL  := 0;
END_VAR

END_FUNCTION_BLOCK

PROGRAM MAIN
VAR
Data  : ARRAY[1 .. 20] OF BOOL;
Ready : BOOL;
CollectInput : F_CollectInput;
END_VAR
VAR
TICK     : BOOL;
IN1      : BOOL;
IN2      : BOOL;
IN3      : BOOL;
IN4      : BOOL;
IN5      : BOOL;
OutReady : BOOL := FALSE;
FeedNext : BOOL := FALSE;
Out      : BOOL;
END_VAR

END_PROGRAM
